        "agent_response": "I can confirm I have the documentation in this conversation. To be precise about what's actually here, I can see:\n\n- **Change-control checklist — platform facilities**: pre-change requirements (named owner, rollback step written by someone else, interlocks and mitigations, named room/rack, second-engineer sign-off with electrical-team reviewer for power distribution changes).\n- **Structure of a note**: customer-facing note format (observable impact → what's being done and by whom → next update), internal notes with working theory and excluded diagnostics, postmortem rules (S1 and repeat S2, blameless, max three actions with owner and date), and the written-handover requirement.\n- **Standing notes**: twice-per-shift walking rounds with recorded times, monthly timestamp sampling, and construction-room exclusions tied to permit validity.\n- **Export reading guide — riser assembly extracts**: headerless, one record per line, family named on the first line, with field order per family (third-riser, north-riser, low-voltage distribution, roof plant) and the warning that the two riser families share a shape but not an order.\n- **Note on scope**: the loop is covered as an asset; pumps and AHUs are not.\n\nOne caveat: several sections are present only as headings with no content — \"During the change\", \"Escalation touchpoints\", \"Out of hours\", and \"Field notes\". If you expected detail under those, it didn't come through, and I won't be able to answer questions about them.",
